      "title": "Scope of the rotational-symmetry classification at sizes 153 and 154",
      "summary": "The half-turn and quarter-turn restrictions are established, but the broader arbitrary-center classification of all nontrivial rotational symmetry at sizes 153 and 154 is incompletely justified because other finite-order lattice rotations are not explicitly excluded. Independently, rct4 is a strict subclass of centered half-turn configurations. This is a qualified scope finding, not a dispute.",
